    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 by WI-tumog's sweep of scripts/ for the sys.path-insertion mechanism (branch jgstern-agent/fix/tumog). The opposite half of WI-tumog's defect: these scripts READ OR WRITE FILES IN THEIR OWN TREE but take hypergumbo's CODE from whatever the interpreter resolves, so run from a worktree (or clone) without PYTHONPATH they pair the worktree's files with the MAIN checkout's code (the editable install's .pth entries).\n\n1. scripts/generate-schema lines 27-29: `sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_ROOT / \"src\"))`. REPO_ROOT/src does not exist (the code moved to packages/*/src), so the insert is dead and hypergumbo_core comes from PYTHONPATH or the editable install. It then writes (or, with --check, compares) REPO_ROOT/docs/schema.json. From a worktree with no PYTHONPATH that is the worktree's schema.json generated from the main checkout's dataclasses. The decontend AGENT_PROMPT's \"pin PYTHONPATH before git commit\" instruction is the manual workaround for exactly this.\n2. scripts/regenerate-backend-agreement-table lines 38-50: no pin at all; imports hypergumbo_core.cli from the interpreter, reads fixtures from REPO_ROOT/packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer, writes REPO_ROOT/docs/audits/0019-....md.\n\nNOT CHECKED: whether any committed docs/schema.json or 0019 table was ever generated from a mismatched tree; I did not run either script from a worktree. The other sys.path-insert scripts (check-*, generate-concept-axes, generate-catalogues-doc, yaml-catalog-index, coverage-select, compute_probe_embeddings.py, generate-architecture) DO pin their own tree's core first, so they are self-consistent at the script level; their core modules' transitive imports were not audited.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (not built): pin the own tree the way the WI-tumog scripts do (scripts/measure_code_tree.py pin(..., \"core\") + announce), or at minimum replace the dead REPO_ROOT/src with packages/hypergumbo-core/src."  # 3dc2
    fields: {}  # 3dc2
